 "obstruction": "All balanced signed ticks reduce to the same B=diag(z,z^-1)J modulo 2. B^t=(z+z^-1)^(t-1) B in F2[z]/(z^N-1). A primitive odd-order root of order dividing N makes this nonzero on either input coin. Thus no positive even-depth column can be a normalized basis mode; odd depth would require an irrational numerator. On an even ring every tick flips site parity. These obstructions concern exact success with no postselection.",
 "scope": "No result for inhomogeneous routing on a lone power-of-two ring of size >=16. Homogeneous nonperiodicity outside sizes 2,4,8 is known; the finite table only checks 48 ticks. The intermodule connector is an added local operation and is not part of the original isolated ring.",
 "homogeneous_period_reference": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1504.06396"
